The Euler–Lagrange equations say $\frac{d}{dt}\frac{\partial L}{\partial\dot q_i}
 =\frac{\partial L}{\partial q_i}.$ Since the derivative on the left is $\dot p_i$, we arrive at $\boxed{
 \dot q_i=\frac{\partial H}{\partial p_i},
 \qquad
 \dot p_i=-\frac{\partial H}{\partial q_i}.}$

