p.src:
Suppose $H(q,p)$ has no explicit time dependence. Along a trajectory, $\begin{aligned}
 \frac{dH}{dt}
 &=\sum_i\left(
 \frac{\partial H}{\partial q_i}\dot q_i
 +\frac{\partial H}{\partial p_i}\dot p_i
 \right) \notag\\
 &=\sum_i\left(
 \frac{\partial H}{\partial q_i}
 \frac{\partial H}{\partial p_i}
 -\frac{\partial H}{\partial p_i}
 \frac{\partial H}{\partial q_i}
 \right)=0.
 \end{aligned}$ The cancellation is pairwise, so $\boxed{H=\text{constant along the motion}.}$

