p.src:
Energy is not the only quantity that may be conserved. Let $A(q,p)$ be any function on phase space. Angular momentum in a plane is one example: $L_z=xp_y-yp_x.$ For an observable with no explicit time dependence, the chain rule and Hamilton’s equations give $\begin{aligned}
 \frac{dA}{dt}
 &=\sum_i\left(
 \frac{\partial A}{\partial q_i}\dot q_i+
 \frac{\partial A}{\partial p_i}\dot p_i
 \right) \notag\\
 &=\sum_i\left(
 \frac{\partial A}{\partial q_i}
 \frac{\partial H}{\partial p_i}
 -
 \frac{\partial A}{\partial p_i}
 \frac{\partial H}{\partial q_i}
 \right).
 \end{aligned}$

