p.src:
This combination is the Poisson bracket. With the convention used here, $\boxed{
 \{A,B\}
 =\sum_i\left(
 \frac{\partial A}{\partial q_i}
 \frac{\partial B}{\partial p_i}
 -
 \frac{\partial A}{\partial p_i}
 \frac{\partial B}{\partial q_i}
 \right).}$ Consequently, $\boxed{\dot A=\{A,H\}.}$ The Hamiltonian is the generator of time evolution.

